wb-docker-app (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Shared lifecycle helper for containerized services on
    Wiren Board controllers, installed once as a dependency by each service:
    - the dedicated `wb` docker network + mosquitto gateway listener +
      net.ipv4.ip_nonlocal_bind, provisioned lazily (opt-in) by the first
      bridge service that needs the broker;
    - the templated systemd unit wb-docker-app@<app>.service (docker compose
      up/down per instance);
    - seed-if-absent of the user layer under /mnt/data and refresh of
      package-owned code (e.g. a service's vendored palette);
    - enabling a service's nginx site (absolute-target symlink) and a tolerant
      proxy reload;
    - excluding the managed packages from unattended-upgrades (updates stay
      explicit);
    - CLI verbs: provision-mqtt, install <app> [--data-uid], remove, reload-proxy.

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0300
